<title>HONG KONG: Bk of E.Asia sees no U.S. rate rises H1.</title>
<headline>Bk of E.Asia sees no U.S. rate rises H1.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of East Asia Ltd deputy chairman and chief executive David Li said on Monday he did not expect United States interest rates to rise in the first half of this year.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe U.S. interest rate will not rise in the first half. I think it will rise no more than half a percentage point in the second half,&quot; Li told a news conference.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
